  "yielded_fraction_note": "KEY PHYSICS: plastic OFFSET persists ~90-98% of steps (kinematic hardening leaves a permanent drift once any story has yielded), but ACTIVE plastic FLOW -- the instants the tangent is actually softened to alpha*k -- occupies only ~0.03-3.8% of steps (uncontrolled). This is WHY the online active-flow-scheduled controllers (GS_LQR_oracle, SA_MPC_oracle) barely differ from the elastic baseline (they only re-tune during those rare flow instants), yet the FIXED softened-DESIGN gain wins: it anticipates the softened mode the structure repeatedly visits at the peaks WITHOUT needing to detect the transient flow. The 1/sqrt(alpha) gain is captured by the DESIGN-frequency choice, not by online switching.",
  "BOTTOM_LINE": "CONSTRUCTIVE POSITIVE: the softening-aware controller 'LQR_softened_design' beats BOTH the tuned elastic LQR (mean margin +0.0900 J over 10/10 cases, worst case +0.0058) and the fixed constrained MPC (mean margin +0.2288 J). The win IS specifically the softened design-frequency: the best plain-DETUNED elastic LQR (best q,r over the grid) only reaches mean J=0.8452, WORSE than the softening-aware 0.7552 -- merely backing off the elastic gain does not recover it, so the gain comes from re-pointing the design to w_s=w1*sqrt(alpha), not from gain magnitude. The 1/sqrt(alpha) insight is constructively exploitable as a new, better controller."
